it was a rare announcement from iran's  atomic agency chief mohammed islami  commence which echo those made recently  by another senior government figure  it is no secret that we have become a  nuclear threshold state and this is a  reality it is also no secret that we  have the technical capabilities required  to manufacture a nuclear bomb  it would be an advancement of iran's  nuclear program far beyond the limits  outlined in a 2015 deal with the west i  am announcing today a deal abandoned by  former u.s president donald trump  at the united nations conference on  non-proliferation u.s secretary of state  anthony blinken criticized iran's  nuclear policy  iran remains on a path  of nuclear escalation  although it publicly claims to favor a  return to mutual compliance with the  jcpoa the joint comprehensive plan of  action  since march  iran has been either unwilling or unable  to accept a deal to achieve precisely  that goal  talks aimed at returning to the deal  have been stalled since march earlier  this week eu foreign policy chief joseph  burrell encouraged both sides to restart  negotiations putting a new proposed text  on the table  after reviewing the draft text it is  possible that in the near future we can  reach a conclusion regarding the time  table for the negotiations we will  probably see a new round of negotiations  negotiations to salvage the nuclear  accord began in april 2021 but have been  in deadlock since february  iran wants the u.s to lift all economic  sanctions and an assurance that the next  administration won't back out of the  accord but the biden administration says  guaranteeing the deal's survival beyond  2024 is impossible  and it wants confirmation that iran  won't enrich uranium to military grade  ali hashem al jazeera
 

